                "id": 944511485942332,
                "preferredName": "Avery Yearwood",
                "firstName": "Avery",
                "lastName": "Yearwood"
            }
        ],
        "abstract": "With three case studies, this paper argued that behind those weird alterations of standard texts, there were good intentions to perfect standard texts. Nevertheless, by mistaking a near jargon, misquotation occurred. The source of misquotation and root cause behind the failure of correction were speculated. A more open and inclusive information sharing mechanism on the formation of standard texts was then advocated as a practicable solution.",
